      { q: 'Why is my Tesla charging at only 16 or 24 amps instead of 48 amps?', a: 'This occurs when line voltage drops below 208V, when internal thermal sensors throttle current to protect the unit from melting, or when configuration settings were lost. We measure impedance and restore full 48A speed.' },
      { q: 'Can you replace a damaged Tesla charging cable or handle?', a: 'Yes! We carry replacement cables, handles with charge port release buttons, and internal contactor boards to repair damaged Wall Connectors without requiring full unit replacement.' },
      { q: 'How fast can an electrician arrive in Los Gatos for a Tesla charger repair?', a: 'Our dispatch center is located at 14165 Capri Drive in Los Gatos. We offer same-day priority service with typical arrival times of 30 to 60 minutes.' },
      { q: 'Do you provide warranties on Tesla charger repairs?', a: 'Yes. All of our repair work and replacement parts are backed by a comprehensive 1-year parts and craftsmanship warranty.' }
    ]
  },
  'level-2-charger-installation': {
    tagline: 'Expert 240-volt Level 2 home charging station diagnostics, component repairs, and circuit troubleshooting across Los Gatos.',
    scope: [
      'Comprehensive diagnostic fault testing for ChargePoint, JuiceBox, Rivian, Autel, Emporia, Wallbox, and Ford Pro stations',
      'Repair and replacement of damaged J1772 and NACS charging handles, latch mechanisms, and pins',
      'Troubleshooting nuisance GFCI breaker trips, false ground faults, and vehicle handshake failures',
      'Replacement of overheated, melted, or loose 240V NEMA 14-50 wall receptacles with industrial Hubbell outlets',
