      { q: 'Can you repair a broken J1772 or NACS charging plug?', a: 'Yes. If the plastic latch is snapped or the connector pins are pitted and burned, we can replace the connector head and cable assembly without replacing the entire charging station.' },
      { q: 'Do you service all brands of Level 2 chargers?', a: 'Yes! We repair ChargePoint Home Flex, JuiceBox, Rivian Wall Chargers, Autel MaxiCharger, Wallbox Pulsar Plus, Emporia, and Ford Charge Station Pro.' },
      { q: 'How long does a typical EV charger repair take?', a: 'Most on-site diagnostic and component repairs are completed within 1 to 2 hours on our initial visit.' }
    ]
  },
  'ev-charger-circuit-panel-upgrade': {
    tagline: 'Comprehensive troubleshooting and repair for tripping EV charging breakers, overheated electrical panels, and overloaded circuits in Los Gatos.',
