      { q: 'Can I reset a tripped EV charger breaker myself?', a: 'You can safely reset it once. If it trips again within 15 to 30 minutes, stop resetting it. Continuous tripping signifies thermal overload, ground faults, or wire insulation breakdown that requires professional diagnostic testing.' },
      { q: 'What is a smart load-shedding switch (DCC-9)?', a: 'A DCC-9 monitors your main panel in real time. If total household power approaches panel capacity, it automatically pauses your EV charger and resumes charging once other appliances turn off, preventing main breaker trips.' },
      { q: 'Why are Zinsco and Federal Pacific panels dangerous for EV chargers?', a: 'Zinsco and Federal Pacific panels have defective breaker clips that loosen under heat. When an EV draws 40+ amps continuously, the connection arcs, melting the busbar and creating a severe fire hazard.' },
      { q: 'Do you provide warranties on panel and breaker repairs?', a: 'Yes. All of our electrical repairs, breaker replacements, and panel components are backed by a 1-year warranty.' }
